# Change Log
All notable changes to this project will be documented in this file.

The format is based on [Keep a Changelog](http://keepachangelog.com/)
and this project adheryou des to [Semantic Versioning](http://semver.org/).

## [Unreleased]

## [Released]
## [1.5.0] - 2026-07-04
### Added
- `operators/layer1-install/values.yaml` — added `cnvOperator` (OpenShift Virtualization / CNV) Subscription entry: package `kubevirt-hyperconverged`, namespace `openshift-cnv`, channel `stable`, source `redhat-operators`, own `OperatorGroup`; **disabled by default** (`enabled: false`)
- `operators/layer2-operands/templates/cnv-hyperconverged.yaml` + `values.yaml` (`cnv`) — `HyperConverged` CR; carries a `kubevirt.kubevirt.io/jsonpatch` annotation forcing `developerConfiguration.useEmulation: true`, required because this cluster's EC2 nodes (`m6a.4xlarge`) are not bare metal and don't expose `/dev/kvm` or vmx/svm CPU flags — AWS only passes hardware virtualization extensions through on `.metal` instance types; **disabled by default** (`enabled: false`)
- `argocd/appset-operators.yaml` — `ignoreDifferences` entry for `HyperConverged` `/status`, since the HCO operator defaults and reconciles most spec fields itself
- `docs/tutorials/openshift-virtualization-on-ec2.md` — new tutorial: why labels/annotations alone can't work around missing hardware virtualization on non-metal EC2, the two real options (bare-metal MachineSet vs. software emulation), and how to verify VMs are running / migrate to bare metal later
- `operators/cleanup-cnv-stale.sh` — teardown script for a previous manual CNV install whose Subscription/CSV had been deleted without uninstalling `HyperConverged` first, orphaning every operand (`virt-*`, `cdi-*`, `kubemacpool-*`, etc.) with no operator left to reconcile them. Deletes the stale webhook configs (`virt-api-validator`, `virt-operator-validator`, `virt-template-validator`, `virt-api-mutator`, `cdi-api-*`) and `APIService` entries (`v1[alpha3].subresources.kubevirt.io`, `v1beta1.upload.cdi.kubevirt.io`) that break namespace-deletion API discovery **cluster-wide**, not just for `openshift-cnv`; strips finalizers nothing will ever clear with the operator gone; and auto-heals CRs that can be orphaned when a namespace's finalizer is force-cleared before all its content finishes deleting
- `.github/workflows/pages.yml` — GitHub Actions workflow building/deploying `docs/` to GitHub Pages via `actions/jekyll-build-pages` + `actions/deploy-pages`

### Changed
- `argocd/appset-workloads.yaml` — re-enabled `get-a-username` (removed from the git-directory generator's exclude list)

## [1.4.0] - 2026-07-04
### Added
- `bases/get-a-username/` — new Kustomize base for the [username-distribution](https://quay.io/openshiftlabs/username-distribution) workshop tool, replacing the old Ansible playbook (`oc process redis-persistent` + `oc new-app --as-deployment-config`) with plain `apps/v1` Deployments, consistent with the rest of this repo (no `DeploymentConfig` anywhere):
  - `redis-pvc.yaml`, `redis-secret.yaml`, `redis-deployment.yaml`, `redis-service.yaml` — Redis backend (1Gi PVC, password-protected)
  - `get-a-username-deployment.yaml`, `get-a-username-service.yaml` — the tool itself, configured entirely via `envFrom` (ConfigMap + Secret), no hardcoded values
  - `init.sh` — idempotent setup script: creates `userN` namespaces + `User` objects + project-scoped `admin` RoleBindings; generates an htpasswd file for `user1`..`userN`; creates/updates the `workshop-htpasswd` Secret (`openshift-config`); merge-patches the `workshop-htpasswd` identity provider into `oauth/cluster` (preserving any other configured IDPs); patches `get-a-username-secret` with the matching password; looks up the real console (and DevSpaces, if installed) route via `oc whoami --show-console` / `oc get routes` and rewrites the tool's "Modules" panel accordingly; restarts the `get-a-username` Deployment so the new ConfigMap/Secret values actually take effect (`envFrom` only injects at container start). The workshop password itself is a plain variable at the top of the file (`WORKSHOP_PASSWORD`, default `CHANGE_ME_BEFORE_RUNNING`) that's edited locally and never pushed back to git — the script refuses to run until it's changed.
  - `cleanup.sh` — full teardown: deletes `userN` namespaces (and legacy `-dev`/`-sit` variants) with `--wait=false` plus a `force_stuck_namespaces` step that safely clears the `kubernetes` finalizer on any namespace left in `Terminating` once its own status confirms all content is already gone (works around namespace deletion getting permanently stuck when another operator's API discovery is broken, e.g. stale KubeVirt/CNV `APIService` entries); deletes `User`/`Identity` objects; removes the `workshop-htpasswd` identity provider from `oauth/cluster` (preserving others) and its Secret. Interactive `y/N` confirmation by default, `-y`/`--yes` to skip.
- `overlay/my-sno-cluster/get-a-username/` — cluster overlay: `kustomization.yaml`, `namespace.yaml` (`guides`), `route.yaml` (edge TLS, empty host), `configmap.yaml` (non-sensitive env: title, duration, user count/prefix, module URLs), `secret.yaml` (placeholder-only — see Security below), `README.md` documenting the full auth + password workflow
- `operators/layer2-operands/templates/workshop-htpasswd.yaml` + `values.yaml` (`workshopAuth`) — cluster-wide `OAuth/cluster` `HTPasswd` identity provider (name `workshop-htpasswd`) so `userN` accounts created by `init.sh` can actually authenticate; without this, `oc create user` only creates orphaned `User` objects with no way to log in. Placed in `layer2-operands` (alongside other cluster-singleton CRs like the ArgoCD CR and RHACS `Central`) rather than in `bases/get-a-username`, since `OAuth/cluster` is cluster-wide — deleting the namespaced workload overlay must never risk also deleting the platform's identity provider config.
- `argocd/appset-operators.yaml` / `argocd/appset-workloads.yaml` — `ignoreDifferences` entries for the `workshop-htpasswd` Secret (`openshift-config`) and `get-a-username-secret` (`guides`), same `Prune=false` + ignore-`/data` pattern already used for the LokiStack S3 secrets

## [1.3.0] - 2026-06-26
### Added
- `operators/layer1-install/values.yaml` — added `netobserv` operator subscription: package `netobserv-operator`, namespace `netobserv`, channel `stable`, source `redhat-operators`, AllNamespaces OperatorGroup (required because `FlowCollector` is a cluster-scoped CRD)
- `operators/layer2-operands/templates/netobserv-lokistack.yaml` — `LokiStack` CR for Network Observability (`netobserv-loki`, namespace `netobserv`, `tenants.mode: openshift-network`); mirrors the logging LokiStack pattern
- `operators/layer2-operands/templates/netobserv-lokistack-s3-secret.yaml` — placeholder S3 secret (`netobserv-loki-s3`) with `argocd.argoproj.io/sync-options: Prune=false`; ArgoCD creates it on first sync but never overwrites after credentials are entered
- `operators/layer2-operands/templates/netobserv-flowcollector.yaml` — `FlowCollector` CR (cluster-scoped singleton, name `cluster`); eBPF agent with features: PacketDrop, DNSTracking, FlowRTT, TLSTracking, PacketTranslation, UDNMapping, IPSec; LokiStack mode pointing to `netobserv-loki`; console plugin, prometheus querier, and 3-replica processor enabled
- `operators/layer2-operands/values.yaml` — added `netobserv` section with `lokiStack` and `flowCollector` subsections; all key FlowCollector settings exposed as values for easy override
- `argocd/appset-operators.yaml` — added `ignoreDifferences` entry for `netobserv-loki-s3` Secret in namespace `netobserv` (same pattern as `logging-loki-s3`)

### Changed
- `operators/layer1-install/values.yaml` — operator version bumps:
  - NVIDIA GPU Operator `v26.3.0` → `v26.3.2` (channel `v26.3` unchanged)
  - Cluster Logging `v6.3.4` / `stable-6.3` → `v6.4.3` / `stable-6.4`
  - Loki Operator `v6.3.4` / `stable-6.3` → `v6.4.3` / `stable-6.4`
  - OpenShift GitOps `v1.20.1` → `v1.20.4` (channel `latest` unchanged)
  - DevWorkspace Operator `v0.40.0` → `v0.41.0` (channel `fast` unchanged)
  - Red Hat OpenShift AI `3.3.0` / `stable-3.3` → `3.4.1` / `stable-3.4`
  - RHACS `v4.10.0` → `v4.11.0` (channel `stable` unchanged)
- `VERSIONS.md` — updated all changed operator rows; added Network Observability row; updated operand versions table

## [1.2.0] - 2026-06-26
### Added
- `bases/ctfd/Makefile` — Helm fetch/template workflow using `pascaliske/ctfd` chart v2.0.0 from `https://charts.pascaliske.dev`; targets: `repo`, `fetch`, `template`
- `bases/ctfd/kustomization.yaml` — base Kustomization referencing pre-rendered `ctfd.yaml`; image override pinning `ghcr.io/ctfd/ctfd` to `3.8.6`; `labels` patch updating `app.kubernetes.io/version` across all resources without touching selectors
- `bases/ctfd/values.yaml` — Helm values with OpenShift-compatible security context (`runAsNonRoot: true` only; no fixed UIDs); `DATABASE_URL` pointing SQLite to PVC-backed `/opt/CTFd/.data/ctfd.db`; PVC subPath mount at `/opt/CTFd/.data` to satisfy CTFd's hardcoded cache/data path
- `bases/ctfd/ctfd.yaml` — pre-rendered Helm manifests (ServiceAccount, Secret, PVC, Service, Deployment)
- `overlay/my-sno-cluster/ctfd/kustomization.yaml` — cluster overlay extending CTFd base
- `overlay/my-sno-cluster/ctfd/namespace.yaml` — `ctfd` namespace
- `overlay/my-sno-cluster/ctfd/route.yaml` — OpenShift Route with TLS edge termination pointing to `ctfd-web` service; hostname auto-assigned by OpenShift
- `overlay/my-sno-cluster/gatus/gatus-config-patch.yaml` — Kustomize strategic merge patch replacing the base `gatus-config` ConfigMap data with full endpoint configuration across 8 groups: Platform Endpoints, Route Endpoints, Logging, Monitoring, Security, External Cluster, Image Repositories, LLM Endpoints
- `overlay/my-sno-cluster/gatus/README.md` — documentation covering FQDN update workflow, adding/removing endpoints, and how the Kustomize patch interacts with `ignoreDifferences`

### Changed
- `argocd/appset-workloads.yaml` — added `allowEmpty: true` to sync policy; removed `resources-finalizer.argocd.argoproj.io` finalizer from template; added `RespectIgnoreDifferences=true` to syncOptions to prevent ArgoCD from overwriting runtime-generated gatus config; excluded `overlay/my-sno-cluster/kyverno` from git directory generator (folder retained for future use)
- `argocd/appset-operators.yaml` — added `allowEmpty: true` to sync policy; removed `resources-finalizer.argocd.argoproj.io` finalizer from template
- `overlay/my-sno-cluster/gatus/kustomization.yaml` — added `patches` entry referencing `gatus-config-patch.yaml`

### Fixed
- **ArgoCD applications stuck deleting** — removed `resources-finalizer.argocd.argoproj.io` from both ApplicationSets so newly created Applications are not blocked from deletion when cluster resources are already gone; added `allowEmpty: true` to prevent sync errors when all managed resources are pruned
- **CTFd SCC violation** — removed hardcoded `runAsUser: 1001`, `runAsGroup: 1001`, `fsGroup: 1001` from `podSecurityContext`; OpenShift's restricted SCC rejects fixed UIDs outside the namespace UID range; pod now inherits a UID from the allowed range
- **CTFd permission denied on `/opt/CTFd/.data`** — CTFd hardcodes its cache and database path to `/opt/CTFd/.data` at import time, ignoring `CACHE_DIR` env var; fixed by mounting the PVC at that exact path via `extraVolumeMounts` subPath `dotdata`

### Removed
- Kyverno excluded from ArgoCD auto-discovery (not deleted); re-enable by removing the exclude entry from `appset-workloads.yaml`

## [1.1.1] - 2026-06-04
### Changed
- Changed Gatus repo pull skeleton
- `bases/gatus/Dockerfile` — switched builder stage from `ubi9/ubi-minimal` to `ubi9/ubi` (full UBI) to gain access to `dnf`; replaced `microdnf --installroot` with `dnf --installroot --setopt=tsflags=noscripts` to skip RPM post-install scriptlets that fail under Rosetta 2 when building `--platform linux/amd64` on Apple Silicon; added manual copy of `tls-ca-bundle.pem` into the rootfs since `update-ca-trust` no longer runs as a scriptlet; bumped `OC_VERSION` default to `4.20.23` and `JQ_VERSION` to `1.8.1`
- `bases/gatus/makefile` — added `vendor` target running `vendir sync`; updated `gatus` helm template target to reference `./vendor/gatus-helmchart` instead of `./`; bumped `GATUS_DISCOVERY_VERSION` to `1.0.0-rc2`
- `bases/gatus/vendir.yml` — added vendir config to sync `https://github.com/betterthanbot/gatus-helmchart.git` at ref `1.0.2` into `vendor/gatus-helmchart/`
- `bases/grafana/dashboard/Admin API & Network Analysis.json` — added `DS_PROMETHEUS` datasource template variable (previously missing entirely); replaced all hardcoded `"datasource": "prometheus"` string literals with proper `{"type": "prometheus", "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"}` objects so the dashboard resolves correctly under the Grafana Operator where datasource UIDs are dynamic
- `bases/grafana/dashboard/RHOAI vLLM Performance Monitor.json` — same datasource fix as above (all panel and variable datasources were hardcoded strings); added `DS_PROMETHEUS` template variable; extended default time range from `now-5m` to `now-1h`
- `bases/grafana/dashboard/vLLM Advanced Performance Dashboard.json` — added `DS_PROMETHEUS` template variable; replaced hardcoded `"uid": "prometheus"` datasource references with `"uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"`; upgraded `schemaVersion` from `36` to `42`
- `bases/grafana/dashboard/README.md` — full rewrite: corrected dashboard count (9, not 10), added quick-reference table with UIDs/refresh/time range, added prerequisites matrix by dashboard, documented `DS_PROMETHEUS` variable behaviour and ACM Right-Sizing exception, expanded per-dashboard panel breakdowns

### Fixed
- `bases/grafana/dashboard/ACM Right-Sizing Namespace.json` — hardcoded `"id": 29` changed to `0`; a non-zero dashboard ID causes import conflicts when provisioning via the Grafana Operator (existing dashboards with the same ID get overwritten)
- `bases/grafana/dashboard/RHOAI GPU Utilization & Consumption.json` — hardcoded `"id": 18` changed to `0`
- `bases/grafana/dashboard/RHOAI Inference Endpoint Monitoring.json` — hardcoded `"id": 16` changed to `0`

## [1.1.0] - 2026-04-19
### Added
- `README.md` — new repo root README covering prerequisites, bootstrap quick start, LokiStack S3 credential setup, RHACS init bundle steps, operator versions table, post-install verification commands, repo structure overview, and links to all docs
- `VERSIONS.md` — operator version reference listing all 11 operators with pinned CSV, channel, source, namespace, and approval mode; includes operand versions and upgrade instructions
- `docs/tutorials/adding-gpu-nodes.md` — new tutorial covering GPU MachineSet provisioning on AWS: cluster value lookup commands, sanitised MachineSet template, GPU instance type reference table, GPU Operator verification steps, and troubleshooting table
- `argocd/appset-operators.yaml` — added `ignoreDifferences` entry for `GrafanaDatasource /spec/datasource/secureJsonData` so ArgoCD does not reset the bearer token injected by the sync-hook Job on each sync

### Changed
- `operators/layer2-operands/templates/grafana-auth-job.yaml` — replaced `valuesFrom` / `kubernetes.io/service-account-token` Secret approach with `oc create token grafana-sa --duration=7440h`; Job now patches `secureJsonData.httpHeaderValue1` directly into every `GrafanaDatasource` CR via `oc patch --type merge`; sync-wave moved from `"1"` to `"3"` so the patch runs after datasource CRs are applied at wave 2
- `operators/layer2-operands/templates/grafana-datasource.yaml` — removed `secureJsonData` and `valuesFrom` from spec; field is intentionally absent from git and injected at runtime by the auth Job
- `operators/layer2-operands/templates/grafana-loki-datasources.yaml` — same removal of `secureJsonData` and `valuesFrom` across all three Loki tenant datasource specs
- `operators/layer2-operands/templates/grafana-serviceaccount.yaml` — updated `grafana-token-builder` Role: added `serviceaccounts/token` create verb; updated secrets verbs to `get`, `create`, `patch`; added `grafanadatasources` get/list/patch; removed the `grafana-sa-token` (`kubernetes.io/service-account-token`) Secret block
- `operators/layer2-operands/templates/rhods-datasciencecluster.yaml` — updated both API versions: `dscinitialization.opendatahub.io/v1` → `v2` and `datasciencecluster.opendatahub.io/v1` → `v2`
- `operators/layer2-operands/values.yaml` (DSCI) — removed `serviceMesh.managementState` field (not present in DSCInitialization v2 schema)
- `operators/layer2-operands/values.yaml` (DSC) — replaced v1 component list with v2 schema: renamed `datasciencepipelines` → `aipipelines`; removed `codeflare` and `modelmeshserving`; added `feastoperator`, `llamastackoperator`, `mlflowoperator`, `modelregistry`, `trainer`; updated `kserve` with `modelsAsService`, `nim`, `rawDeploymentServiceConfig` sub-fields; updated `kueue` with `defaultClusterQueueName`/`defaultLocalQueueName`; updated `workbenches` with `workbenchNamespace`; updated `trustyai` with `eval.lmeval` sub-fields
- `operators/layer2-operands/values.yaml` (NFD) — removed hardcoded `image` field; changed `imagePullPolicy: Always` → `IfNotPresent`; added `servicePort: 12000`; corrected PCI device class from `"02"` → `"0200"`; removed `usb` and `custom` source sections; removed `customConfig` block (field not declared in NFD CRD schema on this cluster)
- `docs/tutorials/grafana-thanos-datasource.md` — fully rewritten to document the CR-patch token injection approach, wave 3 ordering rationale, `ignoreDifferences` explanation, updated architecture diagram, correct resource table, verification steps, and updated troubleshooting table

### Fixed
- **Grafana datasource 401 (Prometheus + Loki)** — root cause: Grafana Operator v5 `valuesFrom` does not reliably inject `secureJsonData`; the operator sends the empty spec value to the Grafana API, clearing any previously stored token. Compounded by wave ordering: the wave-1 Job patch was overwritten when ArgoCD applied datasource CRs at wave 2. Fix: Job moved to wave 3; uses `oc create token grafana-sa --duration=7440h`; patches `secureJsonData.httpHeaderValue1` directly into each `GrafanaDatasource` CR; `ignoreDifferences` on `/spec/datasource/secureJsonData` prevents ArgoCD from resetting it on subsequent syncs
- **NFD pods failing** — `NodeFeatureDiscovery` CR spec contained fields not present in the cluster's NFD CRD schema (`customConfig`) and an incorrect PCI device class whitelist entry (`"02"` should be `"0200"`). Fixed by aligning spec with the default OpenShift NFD operator template
- **OpenShift AI DSC/DSCI sync errors** — templates were using API version `v1` while the installed operator serves `v2`; component names in the DSC spec were v1 names no longer recognised by the v2 CRD. Fixed by updating API versions and component list to match the installed RHOAI 3.3.2 schema

## [1.0.0] - 2026-04-19
### Added
#### GitOps Foundation
- `bootstrap/bootstrap.yaml` — single ArgoCD Application bootstrapping the App-of-Apps pattern; applied once manually to seed the platform
- `argocd/appProject.yaml` — AppProject `openshift4-community` with cluster-wide source/destination access and orphaned resource warnings
- `argocd/appset-operators.yaml` — ApplicationSet (list generator) deploying `operators-layer1` (sync wave 1) and `operators-layer2` (sync wave 2) with `ignoreDifferences` on the LokiStack S3 Secret to prevent credential drift
- `argocd/appset-workloads.yaml` — ApplicationSet (git directory generator) auto-discovering all workloads under `overlay/my-sno-cluster/`; each subdirectory becomes its own ArgoCD Application
- `argocd/rbac-operands.yaml` — ClusterRole + ClusterRoleBinding granting the ArgoCD application controller SA `cluster-admin`; required for managing cluster-scoped resources across all namespaces

#### Operator Layer 1 — `operators/layer1-install/`
Helm chart installing 11 operators via OLM. Each operator entry creates a dedicated Namespace, OperatorGroup, and Subscription. An `enabled:` flag per operator allows zero-downtime enable/disable without touching ArgoCD:
- Grafana Community Operator v5 (`grafana` namespace)
- NVIDIA GPU Operator (`nvidia-gpu-operator` namespace)
- Cluster Observability Operator (`openshift-operators` namespace)
- Compliance Operator (`openshift-compliance` namespace)
- Kernel Module Management (KMM) Hub (`openshift-kmm-hub` namespace)
- Cluster Logging Operator v6 (`openshift-logging` namespace)
- Node Feature Discovery (NFD) (`openshift-nfd` namespace)
- Loki Operator (`openshift-operators-redhat` namespace)
- DevWorkspace Operator (`openshift-operators` namespace)
- RHODS / OpenShift AI (`redhat-ods-operator` namespace)
- RHACS (`stackrox` namespace)

#### Operator Layer 2 — `operators/layer2-operands/`
Helm chart creating operator Custom Resources (operands) once operators are running:
- `grafana-instance.yaml` — `Grafana` CR deploying a community Grafana instance in the dedicated `grafana` namespace
- `grafana-serviceaccount.yaml` — `grafana-sa` ServiceAccount + `grafana-cluster-monitoring-view` ClusterRoleBinding granting read access to OpenShift monitoring metrics
- `grafana-auth-job.yaml` — Sync hook Job (wave 1) that mints a `grafana-sa` bearer token via `oc create token` and writes it to a Secret for use by the datasource
- `grafana-datasource.yaml` — `GrafanaDatasource` CR (wave 2) pointing to `https://thanos-querier.openshift-monitoring.svc:9091` with `valuesFrom` token injection from the Job-written Secret
- `lokistack.yaml` — `LokiStack` CR configured for AWS S3 (`gp3-csi` storage, `1x.pico` size, 14-day log retention)
- `lokistack-s3-secret.yaml` — Placeholder `logging-loki-s3` Secret with `argocd.argoproj.io/sync-options: Prune=false`; ArgoCD creates it on first sync but never deletes or overwrites it after credentials are entered
- `logging-collector-sa.yaml` — `logging-collector` ServiceAccount, `logging-collector-token` Secret (type `kubernetes.io/service-account-token`) providing a long-lived bearer token for the vector log collector, and four ClusterRoleBindings: `collect-application-logs`, `collect-infrastructure-logs`, `collect-audit-logs`, `logging-collector-logs-writer`
- `logging-clusterlogforwarder.yaml` — `ClusterLogForwarder` routing application, infrastructure, and audit logs to LokiStack via the `logging-collector` SA
- `logging-uiplugin.yaml` — `UIPlugin` CR enabling the **Observe → Logs** tab in the OpenShift Web Console (powered by LokiStack)
- `nfd-instance.yaml` — `NodeFeatureDiscovery` CR
- `rhacs-central.yaml` — RHACS `Central` CR
- `rhacs-securedcluster.yaml` — RHACS `SecuredCluster` CR
- `compliance-scansettings.yaml` — two `ScanSetting` CRs (default + scheduled daily)
- `compliance-scansettingbindings.yaml` — two `ScanSettingBinding` CRs (ocp4-cis-1-7 + rhcos4-cis-1-7 profiles)
- `gpu-clusterpolicy.yaml` — NVIDIA GPU `ClusterPolicy` CR enabling GPU feature discovery and device plugin
- `rhods-datasciencecluster.yaml` — `DSCInitialization` + `DataScienceCluster` CRs for OpenShift AI / RHODS
- `gitops-argocd.yaml` — `ArgoCD` CR (disabled by default; managed for completeness)
- `gitops-appprojects.yaml` — additional `AppProject` CRs

#### Workloads
- `overlay/my-sno-cluster/gatus/` — Kustomize overlay for Gatus uptime monitoring with auto-created `gatus` namespace
- `overlay/my-sno-cluster/grafana/` — Kustomize overlay deploying `GrafanaDashboard` CRs to the `grafana` namespace (custom dashboards: cluster health, GPU utilization, vLLM performance, API network analysis, VPA, RHOAI inference)
- `overlay/my-sno-cluster/kyverno/` — Kustomize overlay for Kyverno policy engine with auto-created `kyverno` namespace

#### Documentation — GitHub Pages (`docs/`)
- `docs/_config.yml` — Just the Docs Jekyll theme with hierarchical sidebar navigation and dark color scheme
- `docs/index.md` — Platform home page with navigation to all docs and tutorials
- `docs/platform-docs.md` — Platform Docs parent navigation page
- `docs/architecture.md` — App-of-apps design diagram, sync wave ordering table, two-layer operator model, workload overlay pattern, namespace layout, RBAC model, key design decisions
- `docs/getting-started.md` — Prerequisites (cluster + tooling), step-by-step bootstrap procedure, LokiStack S3 secret setup, verification commands, access URLs, uninstall procedure
- `docs/tutorials/index.md` — Tutorials parent navigation page
- `docs/tutorials/operator-management.md` — Full operator table with enable/disable flags, step-by-step enable/disable/add workflows, version pinning, channel changes, Compliance profile management
- `docs/tutorials/adding-a-workload.md` — Kustomize overlay pattern (Option A) and Helm chart base (Option B), cluster-specific patches, `ignoreDifferences` for runtime-generated fields, verification commands, removal procedure
- `docs/tutorials/grafana-thanos-datasource.md` — Grafana SA token injection mechanism, Thanos datasource GitOps setup, verify and troubleshoot guide
- `docs/tutorials/lokistack-s3-setup.md` — Web Console and CLI methods for entering S3 credentials, LokiStack readiness verification, troubleshooting table

### Changed
- `bootstrap/bootstrap.yaml` — branch updated from `feature/status` → `main`; added cascade deletion finalizer and auto-sync policy
- `argocd/appProject.yaml` — added `orphanedResources` warning configuration
- `argocd/appset-workloads.yaml` — generator `revision` aligned with source `targetRevision` (`feature/reorg`) to correctly discover workload overlay directories on the active branch
- `operators/layer2-operands/values.yaml` — Grafana resources moved from `openshift-operators` to dedicated `grafana` namespace; LokiStack configured for AWS (`gp3-csi`, `1x.pico`, 14-day retention); `uiPlugin` section added for console Logs tab
- `operators/layer2-operands/templates/grafana-auth-job.yaml` — removed `--audience` flag from `oc create token`; confirmed unnecessary on this cluster
- `overlay/my-sno-cluster/gatus/kustomization.yaml` — added `namespace.yaml` resource for auto namespace creation
- `docs/tutorials/grafana-thanos-datasource.md` — updated all namespace references from `openshift-operators` → `grafana` to reflect current deployment

### Fixed
- **Grafana datasource 401** — Grafana `GrafanaDatasource` `valuesFrom` secret reference failed silently when the secret was in a different namespace (`openshift-operators`) than the Grafana instance (`grafana`). Fixed by consolidating all Grafana resources into the `grafana` namespace.
- **ArgoCD workload discovery** — generator `revision: main` caused ArgoCD to discover stale directories (`patches`, `policies`, `vpa`) from the main branch instead of the active `feature/reorg` directories (`gatus`, `grafana`, `kyverno`). Fixed by aligning generator revision with source revision.
- **Vector log collector 403 from LokiStack gateway** — vector reads its bearer token from a directory-mounted Secret (`logging-collector-token`) rather than the pod's projected SA token. Without a `kubernetes.io/service-account-token` type Secret of that name, vector sent no token → 403 Forbidden. Fixed by adding the Secret to `logging-collector-sa.yaml`.
- **ArgoCD forbidden on standard K8s resources** — ArgoCD SA lacked permissions to create Services, Deployments, Routes, and CronJobs for workload apps. Fixed by adding a `cluster-admin` ClusterRoleBinding in `rbac-operands.yaml`.
- **Gatus missing namespace** — Gatus overlay had no namespace; pods could not be scheduled. Fixed by adding `namespace.yaml` to the gatus overlay.
- **LokiStack schema effectiveDate** — admission webhook rejected a future-dated `effectiveDate`; reverted to `"2024-01-01"`.

### Removed
- `argocd/applicationSet.yaml` — replaced by `appset-workloads.yaml` + `appset-operators.yaml`
- `argocd/application.yaml` — superseded by ApplicationSets
- `overlay/my-sno-cluster/kustomization.yaml` — split into per-component subdirectories (`gatus/`, `grafana/`, `kyverno/`)
- cert-manager operator — OpenShift provides equivalent certificate management by default
- Service Mesh operator — OpenShift provides equivalent by default

